            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "redfish/account_service/test_user_account.robot",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "If you are looking to combine it, best is to use Template structure for this for cleaner and optimize code flow\n\nExample:\n\n\nTest Redfish Users Persistency After Reboot\n    [Documentation]  Verify Redfish admin user persistence after reboot.\n    [Tags]  Test_Redfish_Users_Persistency_After_Reboot\n    [Teardown]  Test Teardown Execution\n    [Template]  Verify Redfish User Persistence After Reboot\n\n    # Users                 Role\n    admin_user              Administrator\n    operator_user           Operator\n    readonly_user           ReadOnly\n                       \n*** Keywords ***\n\nVerify Redfish User Persistence After Reboot\n    [Documentation]  Verify Redfish user persistence after reboot.\n    [Arguments]  ${user_name}     ${role}\n    \n    Redfish.Login\n\n    Redfish Create User  ${user_name}   TestPwd123  ${role}  ${True}  \n\n    # Reboot BMC.\n    Redfish OBMC Reboot (off)  stack_mode=normal\n\n    # Verify users after reboot.\n    Redfish Verify User  ${user_name}   TestPwd123  ${role}        ${True}\n\n    Redfish.Delete  /redfish/v1/AccountService/Accounts/${user_name}"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish/account_service/test_user_account.robot",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sridevi Ramesh",
                        "email": "sridevra@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SrideviRamesh"
                    },
                    "message": "Also we dont have operator user enabled in our environment. We would get a failure for operator not user not present. Need to handle this"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish/account_service/test_user_account.robot",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Igor Kanyuka",
                        "email": "ifelmail@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ifel"
                    },
                    "message": "@sridevra@in.ibm.com I don't think this is a problem. If you take a look at the test, it does not use real users, it creates test users with different roles (Administrator, Operator and ReadOnly) on setup stage, in test body reboots BMC and checks the created users still persist, and on tear down stage removes created test users.\n\n@gkeishin@gmail.com I think this will not do what I want. If I do what I suggest, I will be able to combine code to one block, but not the behavior. What I'm trying to achieve here is - speed up test by eliminating multiple reboots. Currently, the code creates admin_user, reboots BMC, check it exists and removes it, then do the same for operator_user and then for the readonly_user one. What you suggest is to keep the behavior, my change changes the logic - create all the users, reboot once, check they still exist and remove. This way I save time taken by 2 additional reboots."
                }
            ],
